{
  "dom_id": "question-166816",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "To complete another job, Mike bought $4$ identical cans of paint, paying a total of $$95.64.$ Estimate the price of each can of paint by rounding the amount of money to the nearest dollar.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The approximate price of each can of paint is $\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate the price of each can of paint, we need to find an approximation for $95.64÷4.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n95.64\\to 96\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $96$ by $4$ as usual:\n\n$$\n96÷4=24\n$$\n\nTherefore, the approximate price of each can of paint is $$24.$",
